---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../lib/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="KimuDev is the build studio behind the Mekridian family of products — Bejirond, Money Matters Daily, TeredaTrades, and Aman's Travels."
>
  <section class="section page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>About</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        KimuDev is the build studio behind the
        <a href={withBase('work/')}>Mekridian family of products</a> —
        started as the internal team building those products, now
        taking on outside work too.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section about-body">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p>
        We don't sell a single package. Some businesses need a
        working site this month; others need a real system that
        doesn't exist yet. We treat those as genuinely different
        jobs — see <a href={withBase('services/')}>Services</a> for
        how each one actually runs.
      </p>
      <p>
        What we can point to is the work itself: a multilingual
        expense manager built for people running more than one
        business, a personal-finance publication, a live trading
        dashboard, a travel site — all still maintained, not
        abandoned after launch. That's the standard a new project
        gets held to as well.
      </p>
      <p>
        KimuDev sits under <strong>Mekridian</strong>, alongside the
        products in our <a href={withBase('work/')}>work</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
